Original commit body from 47a43fa:

Instead of showing confusing raw symbol IDs like
"python:/path/to/file.py:1-1:file:file", file-level symbols
are now displayed as "<module level>" in:

- cmd_explain (callers and callees)
- cmd_symbols (symbol table)
- cmd_search (search results)
- cmd_test_coverage (test names, hot spots, cold spots)

Added _format_symbol_display_name() helper for consistent formatting.
